<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">18062026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Iran has agreed to reopen the Strait of Hormuz immediately, and the United States to lift its naval blockade, under a fourteen-point memorandum signed electronically in Islamabad.</s> <s>The accord commits Israel to halt its operations in Lebanon at once, though Israel sat outside the room and hasn't said it will comply.</s> <s>Whether a deal that binds a third combatant can actually hold... is the question now.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The United Nations recorded thirty-eight thousand five hundred grave violations against children in conflict last year, the most since the mandate began in nineteen ninety-six.</s> <s>Fourteen thousand children were killed or maimed, a thirty-four percent rise, with Palestine leading every nation and two thousand six hundred Palestinian children killed in Gaza alone.</s> <s>For the first time, the report warns that Israeli settlers, not only state forces, could join its list of shame.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's Lahore High Court has declared the country's stone-crushing industry a public health emergency, citing a death rate of ninety-five percent among workers who breathe crystalline silica dust.</s> <s>Because these labourers are unregistered, they fall outside labour law entirely... no compensation, no medical surveillance, no employer ever held to account.</s> <s>The court has ordered officials in three districts to act where ministries spent years looking away.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Japan is building a national intelligence council and a central bureau, consolidating security agencies that were deliberately kept fragmented ever since nineteen forty-five.</s> <s>That fragmentation was designed by the postwar order to prevent Japanese remilitarization.</s> <s>Officials now cite threats from China and North Korea to justify undoing it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Spain's High Court has opened a corruption probe into former prime minister José Luis Rodríguez Zapatero over a fifty-three million euro airline bailout, the first such case against a former premier in its history.</s> <s>The investigation centres on the twenty twenty-one rescue of the airline Plus Ultra, which Zapatero flatly denies.</s> <s>Prosecutors want him to appear before the court every two weeks.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>New research finds that leaving the European Union depressed British exports to the bloc by twelve percent, and that rejoining the customs union would recover almost none of it.</s> <s>Ten of those twelve lost points trace to leaving the single market, not to tariffs, the Centre for European Reform concluded.</s> <s>That's the awkward arithmetic beneath every soft Brexit promise... the fix on offer can't undo the damage.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Nigeria, the price of cooking gas has doubled since April, pushing millions of families back to charcoal and firewood.</s> <s>A kilogramme of liquefied petroleum gas rose from eleven hundred naira to two thousand, reversing years of effort to move households toward cleaner fuel.</s> <s>It's a quiet undoing of progress, paid for in smoke-filled kitchens and felled trees.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>At the G7 summit in Évian, France's Emmanuel Macron kept Donald Trump in the room and secured a joint statement on Ukraine and Iran.</s> <s>Trump even signaled openness to letting Russia's oil-sanction waivers lapse, a notable shift.</s> <s>Diplomats cautioned against optimism... he has reversed himself before.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Brazil's Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva told that same gathering, "I was never a leftist," as he pressed his case against steep American tariffs.</s> <s>Behind the line sits Washington's backing for the Bolsonaro family ahead of October's election, days after Jair Bolsonaro's son was sentenced to four years for lobbying for sanctions against his own country.</s> <s>Lula went to argue from agency, not supplication, and warned Trump against meddling in the vote.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>How does novelty keep arising before there are even cells to carry it?</s> <s>Researchers building a pre-cellular molecular system found that maintaining diversity is what lets it keep evolving, preventing it from settling on a single dead-end optimum.</s> <s>Diversity, it turns out, may be the engine that carries chemistry across the threshold toward life itself.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A Danish study of one hundred and forty thousand people concludes that the sharp rise in autism and attention-deficit diagnoses reflects broadened criteria, not a real epidemic.</s> <s>Recent cases carried lower but still above-average genetic risk, exactly what you'd expect when thresholds widen to recognise more people.</s> <s>More diagnoses, in other words, can mean better recognition rather than a disorder spreading.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>As India grows hotter, breathable cotton has become a tool of survival, yet for many Dalit families it costs double what they can afford.</s> <s>Nearly seventy percent of India's sewer and sanitation workers come from oppressed castes, and they're left in heat-trapping synthetics while told that adaptation is a personal choice.</s> <s>The same heat, then, is far more dangerous depending on the caste you were born into.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Using CRISPR to screen the genome, scientists have identified a single gene that drives the spread of melanoma, the deadliest skin cancer.</s> <s>Blocking that gene with a compound cut tumour spread in mice and outperformed a treatment human researchers had designed by hand.</s> <s>No human trials have begun, but the method hints at letting the genome itself point to its own weak spots.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Apple says it will raise prices because the artificial-intelligence boom has made memory chips, in chief executive Tim Cook's word, unsustainable to source.</s> <s>Demand from AI data centres has more than doubled memory prices since October, as the largest companies outbid makers of phones and laptops for the very same components.</s> <s>The lesson reaches every pocket... the AI build-out isn't free, and ordinary buyers worldwide are quietly footing part of the bill.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A hacking group has published internal data from Madison Square Garden that includes home addresses, talent fees, and risk ratings labelling individuals low or high risk.</s> <s>The venue, already infamous for using facial recognition to eject lawyers from rival firms, had quietly been scoring the very people it tracked.</s> <s>A single breach made visible what corporate surveillance usually keeps hidden... and the hackers say the files can be deleted, for a price.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Britain's National Cyber Security Centre says hostile states are behind three-quarters of attacks on its critical infrastructure and are prepositioning inside power, water and telecoms networks.</s> <s>These intrusions aren't theft, its chief Richard Horne warned... they're target packages for a future war, since strikes tomorrow will rest on intelligence gathered today.</s> <s>He named no states, leaving the question of who is mapping the wires hanging in the air.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>